  "term": "sleep–wake schedule disorder",
  "definition": "Sleep–wake schedule disorder is a circadian sleep problem in which a person’s normal 24-hour sleep–wake pattern is disrupted. It can occur because of travel, shift work, or other causes that disturb usual timing of sleep and wakefulness.",
